# Raw assessment extracts the ETL reads. Not redistributable and not needed to
# build the site — `public/data/` below is the ETL's committed output.
etl/data/

# NOTE: `public/data/facilities/` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# The 2,804 per-facility shards are generated by `npm run data:refresh`, so
# treating them as build output and ignoring them is the intuitive call — but
# the ETL's input (`etl/data/`) is ignored above and absent from the repo, so
# nothing in CI can regenerate them. Netlify runs `npm run build`, which does
# not invoke the ETL at all; it only copies `public/` into `dist/`.
#
# Ignored, the deploy therefore ships a `dist/` with no facility shards, and
# every Scorecard route 404s while the rest of the dashboard looks healthy.
# The generated data is committed instead, and refreshed by re-running the ETL
# locally and committing the diff. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
emr-readiness-by-state.csv
